# ML System Design

## 1. Components of an ML System
- Data Ingestion: Batch (Airflow, Spark) vs Streaming (Kafka, Flink).
- Data Storage: Data Lakes (S3), Data Warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery), Feature Stores (Feast).
- Model Training: Distributed training (Horovod, PyTorch DDP).
- Model Serving: Online (Real-time inference using FastAPI, Triton), Offline (Batch inference), Edge.

## 2. Architectures
- Lambda Architecture: Separate batch and speed layers.
- Kappa Architecture: Everything is a stream.

## 3. MLOps Principles
- Model Monitoring: Concept drift, Data drift.
- CI/CD for ML: Automated testing, model registry (MLflow).
- A/B Testing, Canary Deployment, Shadow Deployment.
